findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    reviewer flagged silent error swallowing in formatters but not in config loading.
    TEA tests config loading but none test that parse/permission errors are distinguished
    from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA''s security_test.rs includes ''CWE-209: Error messages don''t leak
    file paths, connection strings, or stack traces'' and ''all CliError variants
    produce non-empty messages''. However, the reviewer also flagged related concerns
    about SiemClient panics leaking details, though not the exact CliError Display
    issue. Partial catch by TEA.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in siem_client_test.rs (lines 104-141)\
    \ and security_test.rs (lines 39-62) covering CWE-113 for tenant IDs. However,\
    \ the reviewer noted these tests are vacuous (Ok branch doesn't fail), and the\
    \ dev used assert! (panic) rather than validated TenantId from axiathon-core.\
    \ The core issue \u2014 using raw String instead of TenantId \u2014 was not caught."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    inheritance pattern issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''Config silently accepts unknown fields
    (no deny_unknown_fields)'' and specifically called out the token scenario: ''a
    token = "my-secret" field is silently swallowed with no warning''.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged the vacuous test in the same finding as I4: ''the test
    client_config_does_not_have_token_field at config_loading_test.rs:127-138 has
    zero assertions and would pass regardless of behavior. This is a vacuous test.'''
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged the vacuous test pattern: ''has zero assertions and
    would pass regardless of behavior'' referring to config_loading_test.rs:127-138
    which matches the ''let _ = config; test has no assertions'' finding.'
